cid="WO-1997003746-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>WO</country><doc-number>1997003746</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1201609A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>JAPAN SCIENCE &amp; TECH CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MA DENPEI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAEKAWA TAKAAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JAPAN SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MA, DENPEI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAEKAWA, TAKAAKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MA DENPEI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAEKAWA TAKAAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MA, DENPEI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAEKAWA, TAKAAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An oxidatively destructing apparatus comprises anodes each integrally provided with a conductive oxide on its surface and made of a metal, cathodes of a metal plate to which a noble metal is fused, a first chamber (1) housing the anode (1A) and the cathode (1B), a second chamber (2) housing the anode (2A) and the cathode (2B), a partition (20) made of a porous ceramic or resin between the anodes (1A, 2A), and a rectangular wave discharging device for applying an electric field to the first and second chambers. Polluted water fed by a pump (P1) is made to flow through the first chamber (1) and subjected to the electric field.  The supernatant in a settling tank (3) is made to flow through the second chamber (2) by a pump (P2) and subjected to the electric field. As a result, soluble COD, ammonia nitrogen, and nitrate nitrogen are efficiently oxidatively destructed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un appareil de destruction par oxydation, qui présente des anodes comportant chacune un oxyde conducteur intégré à sa surface et constitué d'un métal, des cathodes d'un revêtement métallique auquel un métal noble est fusionné, une première chambre (1) logeant l'anode (1A) et la cathode (1B), une deuxième chambre (2) logeant l'anode (2A) et la cathode (2B), une cloison (20) en céramique poreuse ou résine disposée entre les anodes (1A, 2A), et un dispositif rectangulaire de décharge d'onde pour appliquer un champ électrique sur la première et la deuxième chambres. De l'eau polluée alimentée par une pompe (P1) est amenée à s'écouler à travers la première chambre (1) et soumise au champ électrique. Le supernageant placé dans un bac de décantation (3) est amené à s'écouler à travers la deuxième chambre (2) par une pompe (P2) et soumise au champ électrique, ce qui permet de détruire efficacement, par oxydation, le COD soluble, l'azote ammoniacal et l'azote des nitrates.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>